Demo source and data notices
===========================

The runtime adapters and vendored modules are associated with these projects:

- deid: https://github.com/stelioszach03/deid-privacy-studio
- fraud-graph: https://github.com/stelioszach03/graph-fraud-command-center
- mta-scan: https://github.com/stelioszach03/NYC-Subway-Anomaly-Detection
- smt-verify: https://github.com/stelioszach03/llm-smt-verifiable-reasoning

Each service's LICENSE.upstream preserves its project's original MIT notice.
Local adapter changes and demonstrations do not imply scientific validation.
Third-party packages retain their own licences.

Leaflet's licence is preserved at
mta-scan/static/vendor/LICENSE.leaflet.txt.
MTA schedule/geometry data and frozen replay provenance are described in
mta-scan/data/SOURCES.md. MTA, OpenStreetMap and CARTO data/tiles retain their
respective terms and attribution. Website MIT licensing does not grant new
rights to those materials.

The fraud checkpoint is an 8,806-byte model trained on synthetic transactions
with labels generated by a rule. Its inclusion is for inspecting the exact
demo inference path, not a claim of real-world fraud-detection accuracy.
No third-party pretrained research model or private dataset is bundled.

The website's thesis, CV and research-image exclusions remain unchanged.

The unmodified Mapbox attribution logo retains Mapbox copyright/trademark
rights and is not covered by the MIT grant. Its source and attribution terms
are preserved in mta-scan/static/vendor/NOTICE.mapbox-logo.txt.
Deployment-only map-config.json and access tokens are not published; only the
blank map-config.example.json template is part of this source tree.
